  "prompt": "A weary World War II American infantryman crouches deep inside a muddy foxhole, rain and dirt smeared across his face. His steel M1 helmet is dented and scratched, rainwater streaking down its surface. His eyes are hollow, exhausted the stare of a man who has seen too much. He grips his M1 Garand tightly, knuckles white, fingertips trembling from cold and adrenaline. Around him, the battlefield is desolate and torn apart splintered trees reduced to charred stumps, earth churned into wet cratered mud, the smoke of distant artillery drifting in heavy gray sheets. The air is wet, cold, suffocating, filled with the smell of soil, cordite, and burning wood. The lighting is muted and natural overcast sky, diffused daylight, everything washed in tones of gray, brown, and olive. Steam rises faintly from his breath in the cold as rain drips into the foxhole. His uniform is soaked, patched, and worn, ammo pouches heavy against his chest, dog tags barely visible beneath layers of grime. The scene is silent except for the distant echo of war, a moment of tension before the next barrage. The mood is grim, brutal, and human survival, fear, and unwavering resolve. --ar 9:16",
